  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers OAuth 2.0 (RFC 6749, RFC 6750) as tightened by the RFC 9700 Security BCP and the OAuth 2.1 draft (-16, build posture), with the extensions a resource server, client or authorization server needs: PKCE, DPoP, mTLS-bound tokens, Rich Authorization Requests, token exchange, resource indicators, AS and protected resource metadata, the iss parameter, step-up, dynamic client registration, introspection, revocation and the device grant. Drafts for Client ID Metadata Documents, identity chaining, transaction tokens and RAR remediation are pinned with a posture. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out the resource server, sender constraint, clients, the authorization server, delegation and drafts.",
